WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.150
In 2024, GDP per head in
London was 72,201 pounds.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:11.370
In the North East, 29,957 pounds.

3
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.370
That's about 2.4 times as much.

4
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:19.210
In 2014, HS2's stated aim
was Rebalancing Britain.

5
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.510
It pointed to what it called our
economic over-reliance on London.

6
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.030
At Heathrow, a north-west
runway is planned.

7
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:31.110
The government says it could deliver
over 40 billion pounds of benefits.

8
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.630
So will a railway and a runway
spread wealth beyond London?

9
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.450
In this mission, you'll test where HS2
and Heathrow's benefits are meant to land,

10
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.830
and when.

11
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.350
Then you'll add three
more levers: planning law,

12
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.970
migration rules and financial rules.

13
00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:52.830
Your mission: assess whether the new
railway and runway will spread wealth beyond

14
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:53.630
London.
